  "body": "(I hope this is the right place to put this — the mailing list I’ve used in the past for messages like this has since been shut down. If there’s a better place, please let me know. Thanks)\r\n\r\n**I propose** adding a `src` attribute to the `svg` element as it is used in HTML to allow embedding of external SVG files within pages. This would differ from using `<img src>` with an SVG file as referent because the SVG file referred to could be styled with CSS rules from the document.\r\n\r\nThat is, given the following HTML snippet:\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<style>\r\nsvg { fill: red; }\r\n</style>\r\n<svg src=\"circle.svg\"></svg>\r\n```\r\n\r\nand the following `circle.svg`:\r\n\r\n```xml\r\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\r\n  <circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"50\" r=\"50\" />\r\n</svg>\r\n```\r\n\r\nthe resulting circle would be red, not the default colour (black).\r\n\r\nThe **intended use case** for this is primarily icons. On the source of this very GitHub page, for instance, you‘ll see dozens of icons embedded as SVG directly instead of linking to them in external files. [GitHub does this because icon fonts are bad for accessibility and embedding the SVG source directly in the HTML is currently the only way to use CSS styling on them.](https://github.blog/2016-02-22-delivering-octicons-with-svg/) (I’m using GitHub as an example as they’re a big website, but I have adopted the same approach on sites I’ve worked on due to exactly the same circumstances.) This seems a waste of bandwidth, since the icons could easily be downloaded once for all page views and then cached for future uses. This bandwidth waste further be improved by allowing use of the `viewBox` attribute on graphics embedded with `<svg src>`, overriding any `viewBox` specified in the linked SVG file. That would allow SVG icon sheets to be made with all the site’s icons in a single file, saving on HTTP requests. For instance, in an icon sheet full of notionally 16px &times; 16px icons, the following would show the second icon in the third row:\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<svg src=\"icon-sheet.svg\" viewBox=\"16 32 16 16\"></svg>\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe other SVG attributes would also continue to work, again overriding any specified in the linked SVG file.\r\n\r\nIf there’s interest in this I’m willing to have a shot at editing the spec to add this feature and making a PR out of it, although I don’t have any clout to get this taken up by implementors (other than just opening bugs on the relevant browser engines’ issue trackers).\r\n",
